<hr data-start=3D"174" data-end=3D"177">
<h1 data-start=3D"179" data-end=3D"243">=F0=9F=93=9A 5.7 =E2=80=94 Signals =
en Django (pr=C3=A9-save, post-save, delete, etc.)</h1>
<hr data-start=3D"245" data-end=3D"248">
<h2 data-start=3D"250" data-end=3D"265">=F0=9F=8E=AF Objectifs</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"267" data-end=3D"655">
<li data-start=3D"267" data-end=3D"337">
<p data-start=3D"269" data-end=3D"337">Comprendre ce que sont les signals d=
ans Django et =C3=A0 quoi ils servent</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"338" data-end=3D"445">
<p data-start=3D"340" data-end=3D"445">Apprendre =C3=A0 utiliser les princi=
paux signals int=C3=A9gr=C3=A9s (pr=C3=A9-save, post-save, pr=C3=A9-delete,=
 post-delete, etc.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"446" data-end=3D"531">
<p data-start=3D"448" data-end=3D"531">Savoir connecter des fonctions aux s=
ignals pour d=C3=A9clencher des actions automatiques</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"532" data-end=3D"609">
<p data-start=3D"534" data-end=3D"609">D=C3=A9couvrir les bonnes pratiques =
d=E2=80=99utilisation des signals et les cas avanc=C3=A9s</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"610" data-end=3D"655">
<p data-start=3D"612" data-end=3D"655">=C3=89viter les pi=C3=A8ges courants=
 li=C3=A9s aux signals</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"657" data-end=3D"660">
<h2 data-start=3D"662" data-end=3D"699">1. Introduction aux Signals Django<=
/h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"701" data-end=3D"733">1.1 Qu=E2=80=99est-ce qu=E2=80=99un=
 signal ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"735" data-end=3D"934">Un <strong data-start=3D"738" data-e=
nd=3D"748">signal</strong> est un m=C3=A9canisme qui permet =C3=A0 certaine=
s parties de votre application Django de <strong data-start=3D"828" data-en=
d=3D"885">r=C3=A9agir automatiquement =C3=A0 certains =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements =
internes</strong> (comme la sauvegarde ou suppression d=E2=80=99un objet).<=
/p>
<p data-start=3D"936" data-end=3D"1070">Les signals agissent comme des =C2=
=AB&nbsp;=C3=A9couteurs&nbsp;=C2=BB (listeners) qui attendent qu=E2=80=99un=
 =C3=A9v=C3=A9nement se produise, puis ex=C3=A9cutent du code en r=C3=A9pon=
se.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1072" data-end=3D"1075">
<h3 data-start=3D"1077" data-end=3D"1116">1.2 Pourquoi utiliser les signals=
 ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1118" data-end=3D"1489">
<li data-start=3D"1118" data-end=3D"1238">
<p data-start=3D"1120" data-end=3D"1238">Pour <strong data-start=3D"1125" d=
ata-end=3D"1138">d=C3=A9coupler</strong> la logique m=C3=A9tier li=C3=A9e =
=C3=A0 certains =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements (ex: envoyer un email apr=C3=A8s cr=C3=
=A9ation d=E2=80=99un utilisateur)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1239" data-end=3D"1312">
<p data-start=3D"1241" data-end=3D"1312">Automatiser des actions sans modif=
ier directement la logique principale</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1313" data-end=3D"1397">
<p data-start=3D"1315" data-end=3D"1397">Ajouter des comportements transver=
saux (logging, cache, mises =C3=A0 jour automatiques)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1398" data-end=3D"1489">
<p data-start=3D"1400" data-end=3D"1489">R=C3=A9agir =C3=A0 des =C3=A9v=C3=
=A9nements du cycle de vie des mod=C3=A8les (cr=C3=A9ation, modification, s=
uppression)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1491" data-end=3D"1494">
<h3 data-start=3D"1496" data-end=3D"1530">1.3 Quand =C3=A9viter les signals=
 ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1532" data-end=3D"1867">
<li data-start=3D"1532" data-end=3D"1682">
<p data-start=3D"1534" data-end=3D"1682">Si la logique peut =C3=AAtre g=C3=
=A9r=C3=A9e directement dans les vues ou les m=C3=A9thodes des mod=C3=A8les=
 (<code data-start=3D"1619" data-end=3D"1625">save</code>, <code data-start=
=3D"1627" data-end=3D"1635">delete</code>), pr=C3=A9f=C3=A9rez cette approc=
he pour plus de clart=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1683" data-end=3D"1779">
<p data-start=3D"1685" data-end=3D"1779">Si trop utilis=C3=A9s, les signals=
 rendent le code difficile =C3=A0 suivre car le flux devient indirect.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1780" data-end=3D"1867">
<p data-start=3D"1782" data-end=3D"1867">Privil=C3=A9gier des services ou t=
=C3=A2ches asynchrones (ex: Celery) pour des actions longues.</p>
</li>
</ul>
