=3D"54">complet et approfondi</strong> sur la cr=C3=A9ation et la gestion d=
es migrations dans Django, allant du niveau d=C3=A9butant au niveau expert.=
</p>
<hr data-start=3D"158" data-end=3D"161">
<h1 data-start=3D"163" data-end=3D"220">=F0=9F=93=9A 6.2 =E2=80=94 Cr=C3=A9=
ation et gestion des migrations dans Django</h1>
<hr data-start=3D"222" data-end=3D"225">
<h2 data-start=3D"227" data-end=3D"242">=F0=9F=8E=AF Objectifs</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"244" data-end=3D"703">
<li data-start=3D"244" data-end=3D"331">
<p data-start=3D"246" data-end=3D"331">Comprendre ce que sont les migration=
s dans Django et pourquoi elles sont essentielles</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"332" data-end=3D"413">
<p data-start=3D"334" data-end=3D"413">Savoir cr=C3=A9er, appliquer, annule=
r, et g=C3=A9rer les migrations dans un projet Django</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"414" data-end=3D"478">
<p data-start=3D"416" data-end=3D"478">Appr=C3=A9hender les bonnes pratique=
s et pi=C3=A8ges li=C3=A9s aux migrations</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"479" data-end=3D"551">
<p data-start=3D"481" data-end=3D"551">Ma=C3=AEtriser les commandes avanc=
=C3=A9es et la personnalisation des migrations</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"552" data-end=3D"633">
<p data-start=3D"554" data-end=3D"633">G=C3=A9rer les migrations dans diff=
=C3=A9rents environnements (d=C3=A9veloppement, production)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"634" data-end=3D"703">
<p data-start=3D"636" data-end=3D"703">Comprendre l=E2=80=99interaction ent=
re les migrations et la base de donn=C3=A9es</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"705" data-end=3D"708">
<h2 data-start=3D"710" data-end=3D"771">1. Introduction : Qu=E2=80=99est-ce=
 qu=E2=80=99une migration dans Django ?</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"773" data-end=3D"776">
<h3 data-start=3D"778" data-end=3D"796">1.1 D=C3=A9finition</h3>
<p data-start=3D"798" data-end=3D"935">Une migration dans Django est un fic=
hier Python qui d=C3=A9crit les modifications =C3=A0 apporter =C3=A0 la str=
ucture de la base de donn=C3=A9es, notamment :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"937" data-end=3D"1092">
<li data-start=3D"937" data-end=3D"986">
<p data-start=3D"939" data-end=3D"986">Cr=C3=A9ation, modification ou suppr=
ession de tables</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"987" data-end=3D"1048">
<p data-start=3D"989" data-end=3D"1048">Ajout, suppression ou modification =
de champs dans un mod=C3=A8le</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1049" data-end=3D"1092">
<p data-start=3D"1051" data-end=3D"1092">Gestion des contraintes, index, re=
lations</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1094" data-end=3D"1097">
<h3 data-start=3D"1099" data-end=3D"1158">1.2 Pourquoi les migrations sont-=
elles indispensables ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1160" data-end=3D"1447">
<li data-start=3D"1160" data-end=3D"1237">
<p data-start=3D"1162" data-end=3D"1237">Elles permettent de synchroniser l=
a base de donn=C3=A9es avec les mod=C3=A8les Python</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1238" data-end=3D"1314">
<p data-start=3D"1240" data-end=3D"1314">Elles assurent la tra=C3=A7abilit=
=C3=A9 et versionnement des modifications de sch=C3=A9ma</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1315" data-end=3D"1385">
<p data-start=3D"1317" data-end=3D"1385">Elles facilitent la collaboration =
en =C3=A9quipe sur le mod=C3=A8le de donn=C3=A9es</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1386" data-end=3D"1447">
<p data-start=3D"1388" data-end=3D"1447">Elles =C3=A9vitent de devoir =C3=
=A9crire manuellement des scripts SQL</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1449" data-end=3D"1452">
<h2 data-start=3D"1454" data-end=3D"1487">2. Cycle de vie des migrations</h=
2>
<hr data-start=3D"1489" data-end=3D"1492">
<h3 data-start=3D"1494" data-end=3D"1518">2.1 Le cycle g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ral</h=
3>
<ol data-start=3D"1520" data-end=3D"1778">
<li data-start=3D"1520" data-end=3D"1567">
<p data-start=3D"1523" data-end=3D"1567">Modifier ou cr=C3=A9er un mod=C3=
=A8le dans <code data-start=3D"1556" data-end=3D"1567">models.py</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1568" data-end=3D"1631">
<p data-start=3D"1571" data-end=3D"1631">G=C3=A9n=C3=A9rer une migration av=
ec <code data-start=3D"1598" data-end=3D"1631">python manage.py makemigrati=
ons</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1632" data-end=3D"1699">
<p data-start=3D"1635" data-end=3D"1699">Appliquer la migration =C3=A0 la b=
ase avec <code data-start=3D"1673" data-end=3D"1699">python manage.py migra=
