<hr data-start=3D"634" data-end=3D"637">
<h2 data-start=3D"639" data-end=3D"684">=F0=9F=A7=A0 I. Comprendre le syst=
=C3=A8me de permissions</h2>
<p data-start=3D"686" data-end=3D"793">Django poss=C3=A8de un <strong data-=
start=3D"704" data-end=3D"752">syst=C3=A8me d'authentification et d'autoris=
ation</strong> int=C3=A9gr=C3=A9 via l'app <code data-start=3D"771" data-en=
d=3D"792">django.contrib.auth</code>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"795" data-end=3D"837">Trois permissions de base par mod=
=C3=A8le :</h3>
<p data-start=3D"839" data-end=3D"912">Quand vous cr=C3=A9ez un mod=C3=A8le=
, Django g=C3=A9n=C3=A8re automatiquement 3 permissions :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"914" data-end=3D"1039">
<li data-start=3D"914" data-end=3D"952">
<p data-start=3D"916" data-end=3D"952"><code data-start=3D"916" data-end=3D=
"933">add_&lt;modelname&gt;</code> : ajouter un objet</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"953" data-end=3D"995">
<p data-start=3D"955" data-end=3D"995"><code data-start=3D"955" data-end=3D=
"975">change_&lt;modelname&gt;</code> : modifier un objet</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"996" data-end=3D"1039">
<p data-start=3D"998" data-end=3D"1039"><code data-start=3D"998" data-end=
=3D"1018">delete_&lt;modelname&gt;</code> : supprimer un objet</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1041" data-end=3D"1075">Exemple pour un mod=C3=A8le <code =
data-start=3D"1064" data-end=3D"1073">Produit</code> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1077" data-end=3D"1130">
<li data-start=3D"1077" data-end=3D"1092">
<p data-start=3D"1079" data-end=3D"1092"><code data-start=3D"1079" data-end=
=3D"1092">add_produit</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1093" data-end=3D"1111">
<p data-start=3D"1095" data-end=3D"1111"><code data-start=3D"1095" data-end=
=3D"1111">change_produit</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1112" data-end=3D"1130">
<p data-start=3D"1114" data-end=3D"1130"><code data-start=3D"1114" data-end=
=3D"1130">delete_produit</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1132" data-end=3D"1169">Depuis Django 2.1+, vous avez auss=
i :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1171" data-end=3D"1244">
<li data-start=3D"1171" data-end=3D"1244">
<p data-start=3D"1173" data-end=3D"1244"><code data-start=3D"1173" data-end=
=3D"1191">view_&lt;modelname&gt;</code> : voir un objet (utile pour les int=
erfaces readonly)</p>
</li>
</ul>
