<p data-start=3D"647" data-end=3D"702">Int=C3=A9grer et configurer ce backe=
nd dans un projet Django</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"703" data-end=3D"753">
<p data-start=3D"705" data-end=3D"753">Tester et utiliser ce backend dans d=
es cas r=C3=A9els</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"754" data-end=3D"813">
<p data-start=3D"756" data-end=3D"813">Explorer des cas avanc=C3=A9s d=E2=
=80=99authentification personnalis=C3=A9e</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"815" data-end=3D"818">
<h2 data-start=3D"820" data-end=3D"885">=F0=9F=A7=B1 I. Qu=E2=80=99est-ce q=
u=E2=80=99un backend d=E2=80=99authentification dans Django ?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"887" data-end=3D"978">Un <strong data-start=3D"890" data-e=
nd=3D"920">backend d=E2=80=99authentification</strong> est une classe Pytho=
n qui d=C3=A9finit la logique permettant :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"980" data-end=3D"1163">
<li data-start=3D"980" data-end=3D"1072">
<p data-start=3D"982" data-end=3D"1072">De v=C3=A9rifier les informations d=
=E2=80=99identification d=E2=80=99un utilisateur (ex : login + mot de passe=
)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1073" data-end=3D"1163">
<p data-start=3D"1075" data-end=3D"1163">De r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9rer un utilisat=
eur =C3=A0 partir d=E2=80=99un identifiant (ex : id, username, email, token=
=E2=80=A6)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1165" data-end=3D"1254">Django utilise ces backends pour v=
alider les connexions via la fonction <code data-start=3D"1237" data-end=3D=
"1253">authenticate()</code>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1256" data-end=3D"1279">Backends par d=C3=A9faut</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1281" data-end=3D"1511">
<li data-start=3D"1281" data-end=3D"1404">
<p data-start=3D"1283" data-end=3D"1404"><code data-start=3D"1283" data-end=
=3D"1326">django.contrib.auth.backends.ModelBackend</code> : utilise le mod=
=C3=A8le <code data-start=3D"1347" data-end=3D"1353">User</code> avec un ch=
amp <code data-start=3D"1368" data-end=3D"1378">username</code> et un mot d=
e passe hach=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1405" data-end=3D"1511">
<p data-start=3D"1407" data-end=3D"1511">Il est possible d=E2=80=99en d=C3=
=A9finir plusieurs et Django va tester chacun jusqu=E2=80=99=C3=A0 trouver =
un utilisateur valide.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1513" data-end=3D"1516">
<h2 data-start=3D"1518" data-end=3D"1568">=F0=9F=94=8D II. Pourquoi cr=C3=
=A9er un backend personnalis=C3=A9 ?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1570" data-end=3D"1605">Voici plusieurs raisons courantes =
:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1607" data-end=3D"2090">
<li data-start=3D"1607" data-end=3D"1669">
<p data-start=3D"1609" data-end=3D"1669"><strong data-start=3D"1609" data-e=
nd=3D"1639">Authentification par email</strong> au lieu du username classiq=
ue</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1670" data-end=3D"1743">
<p data-start=3D"1672" data-end=3D"1743"><strong data-start=3D"1672" data-e=
nd=3D"1716">Authentification via un champ sp=C3=A9cifique</strong> (ex : nu=
m=C3=A9ro de t=C3=A9l=C3=A9phone)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1744" data-end=3D"1829">
<p data-start=3D"1746" data-end=3D"1829"><strong data-start=3D"1746" data-e=
nd=3D"1785">Int=C3=A9gration avec un syst=C3=A8me externe</strong> (LDAP, O=
Auth, SSO, base de donn=C3=A9es externe)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1830" data-end=3D"1886">
<p data-start=3D"1832" data-end=3D"1886"><strong data-start=3D"1832" data-e=
nd=3D"1886">Authentification multi-facteurs ou bas=C3=A9e sur token</strong=
></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1887" data-end=3D"2015">
<p data-start=3D"1889" data-end=3D"2015"><strong data-start=3D"1889" data-e=
nd=3D"1918">Logique m=C3=A9tier sp=C3=A9cifique</strong> pour valider ou re=
jeter une connexion (ex : utilisateurs actifs uniquement, profils sp=C3=A9c=
ifiques)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2016" data-end=3D"2090">
<p data-start=3D"2018" data-end=3D"2090"><strong data-start=3D"2018" data-e=
nd=3D"2065">Support de plusieurs m=C3=A9thodes simultan=C3=A9ment</strong> =
(ex : username ou email)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2092" data-end=3D"2095">
<h2 data-start=3D"2097" data-end=3D"2137">=E2=9A=99=EF=B8=8F III. Structure=
 d=E2=80=99un backend custom</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2139" data-end=3D"2212">Un backend d=E2=80=99authentificat=
ion doit impl=C3=A9menter au minimum deux m=C3=A9thodes :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2214" data-end=3D"2510">
<li data-start=3D"2214" data-end=3D"2373">
<p data-start=3D"2216" data-end=3D"2373"><code data-start=3D"2216" data-end=
=3D"2260">authenticate(self, request, **credentials)</code><br data-start=
=3D"2260" data-end=3D"2263">
Cette m=C3=A9thode re=C3=A7oit les informations d=E2=80=99authentification =
et doit retourner un objet <code data-start=3D"2349" data-end=3D"2355">User=
</code> valide ou <code data-start=3D"2366" data-end=3D"2372">None</code>.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2377" data-end=3D"2510">
<p data-start=3D"2379" data-end=3D"2510"><code data-start=3D"2379" data-end=
=3D"2404">get_user(self, user_id)</code><br data-start=3D"2404" data-end=3D=
"2407">
Cette m=C3=A9thode r=C3=A9cup=C3=A8re un utilisateur =C3=A0 partir de son I=
D et doit retourner un objet <code data-start=3D"2493" data-end=3D"2499">Us=
er</code> ou <code data-start=3D"2503" data-end=3D"2509">None</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
