<hr data-start=3D"228" data-end=3D"231">
<h1 data-start=3D"233" data-end=3D"290">11. Tests en Django =E2=80=94 Intro=
duction compl=C3=A8te et pratique</h1>
<hr data-start=3D"292" data-end=3D"295">
<h2 data-start=3D"297" data-end=3D"347">11.1 Introduction aux tests unitair=
es en Django</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"349" data-end=3D"352">
<h3 data-start=3D"354" data-end=3D"389">Qu=E2=80=99est-ce qu=E2=80=99un tes=
t unitaire ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"391" data-end=3D"610">Un test unitaire est un script ou un=
e fonction qui v=C3=A9rifie qu=E2=80=99une unit=C3=A9 sp=C3=A9cifique de co=
de fonctionne comme attendu. Dans Django, cette unit=C3=A9 peut =C3=AAtre u=
ne vue, un mod=C3=A8le, un formulaire, ou toute autre fonction/m=C3=A9thode=
.</p>
<p data-start=3D"612" data-end=3D"628">L=E2=80=99objectif est :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"630" data-end=3D"780">
<li data-start=3D"630" data-end=3D"664">
<p data-start=3D"632" data-end=3D"664"><strong data-start=3D"632" data-end=
=3D"664">D=C3=A9tecter rapidement les bugs</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"665" data-end=3D"734">
<p data-start=3D"667" data-end=3D"734"><strong data-start=3D"667" data-end=
=3D"734">Garantir que le code continue =C3=A0 fonctionner apr=C3=A8s modifi=
cations</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"735" data-end=3D"780">
<p data-start=3D"737" data-end=3D"780"><strong data-start=3D"737" data-end=
=3D"780">Faciliter la maintenance et l=E2=80=99=C3=A9volution</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"782" data-end=3D"785">
<h3 data-start=3D"787" data-end=3D"818">Pourquoi tester en Django ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"820" data-end=3D"1029">
<li data-start=3D"820" data-end=3D"854">
<p data-start=3D"822" data-end=3D"854">Applications robustes et fiables</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"855" data-end=3D"921">
<p data-start=3D"857" data-end=3D"921">Faciliter le refactoring sans peur d=
e casser des fonctionnalit=C3=A9s</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"922" data-end=3D"981">
<p data-start=3D"924" data-end=3D"981">Automatiser la v=C3=A9rification de =
bugs lors des d=C3=A9ploiements</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"982" data-end=3D"1029">
<p data-start=3D"984" data-end=3D"1029">Documentation vivante du comporteme=
nt attendu</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1031" data-end=3D"1034">
<h3 data-start=3D"1036" data-end=3D"1070">Le framework de test de Django</h=
3>
<p data-start=3D"1072" data-end=3D"1161">Django int=C3=A8gre un framework d=
e test bas=C3=A9 sur Python <code data-start=3D"1124" data-end=3D"1134">uni=
ttest</code> mais adapt=C3=A9 =C3=A0 ses besoins.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1163" data-end=3D"1176">Points cl=C3=A9s :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1178" data-end=3D"1482">
<li data-start=3D"1178" data-end=3D"1247">
<p data-start=3D"1180" data-end=3D"1247">Les tests sont =C3=A9crits dans de=
s fichiers <code data-start=3D"1220" data-end=3D"1230">tests.py</code> dans=
 chaque app.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1248" data-end=3D"1318">
<p data-start=3D"1250" data-end=3D"1318">Les classes de test h=C3=A9ritent =
g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement de <code data-start=3D"1295" data-end=3D"1317">djang=
o.test.TestCase</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1319" data-end=3D"1409">
<p data-start=3D"1321" data-end=3D"1409">Django fournit des outils sp=C3=A9=
cifiques (client de test HTTP, assertions personnalis=C3=A9es=E2=80=A6).</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1410" data-end=3D"1482">
<p data-start=3D"1412" data-end=3D"1482">Les tests peuvent =C3=AAtre lanc=
=C3=A9s via la commande <code data-start=3D"1458" data-end=3D"1481">python =
manage.py test</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1484" data-end=3D"1487">
<h3 data-start=3D"1489" data-end=3D"1515">Organisation des tests</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1517" data-end=3D"1790">
<li data-start=3D"1517" data-end=3D"1591">
<p data-start=3D"1519" data-end=3D"1591"><strong data-start=3D"1519" data-e=
nd=3D"1532">Unitaires</strong> : testent des petites unit=C3=A9s isol=C3=A9=
es (ex : m=C3=A9thode mod=C3=A8le)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1592" data-end=3D"1692">
<p data-start=3D"1594" data-end=3D"1692"><strong data-start=3D"1594" data-e=
nd=3D"1617">Tests d=E2=80=99int=C3=A9gration</strong> : testent plusieurs c=
omposants ensemble (ex : une vue utilisant un mod=C3=A8le)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1693" data-end=3D"1790">
<p data-start=3D"1695" data-end=3D"1790"><strong data-start=3D"1695" data-e=
nd=3D"1730">Tests fonctionnels / end-to-end</strong> (avec Selenium ou autr=
e) : simulent un utilisateur complet.</p>
</li>
</ul>
