<hr data-start=3D"5331" data-end=3D"5334">
<h2 data-start=3D"5336" data-end=3D"5362">11.4 Couverture de code</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"5364" data-end=3D"5367">
<h3 data-start=3D"5369" data-end=3D"5410">Qu=E2=80=99est-ce que la couvertu=
re de code ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"5412" data-end=3D"5531">La couverture de code (code covera=
ge) mesure la proportion de votre code source ex=C3=A9cut=C3=A9e lors de l=
=E2=80=99ex=C3=A9cution des tests.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5533" data-end=3D"5717">
<li data-start=3D"5533" data-end=3D"5606">
<p data-start=3D"5535" data-end=3D"5606">Un bon score de couverture indique=
 que la majorit=C3=A9 du code a =C3=A9t=C3=A9 test=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5607" data-end=3D"5717">
<p data-start=3D"5609" data-end=3D"5717">Attention : la couverture ne garan=
tit pas que les tests soient corrects, seulement qu=E2=80=99ils ex=C3=A9cut=
ent le code.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5719" data-end=3D"5722">
<h3 data-start=3D"5724" data-end=3D"5760">Outils de couverture avec Django<=
/h3>
<p data-start=3D"5762" data-end=3D"5835">Le plus utilis=C3=A9 est <strong d=
ata-start=3D"5782" data-end=3D"5797">coverage.py</strong> qui s=E2=80=99int=
=C3=A8gre facilement avec Django.</p>
