<hr data-start=3D"4455" data-end=3D"4458">
<h4 data-start=3D"4460" data-end=3D"4479">Particularit=C3=A9s</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4481" data-end=3D"4692">
<li data-start=3D"4481" data-end=3D"4552">
<p data-start=3D"4483" data-end=3D"4552">Playwright supporte plusieurs navi=
gateurs (Chromium, Firefox, WebKit)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4553" data-end=3D"4616">
<p data-start=3D"4555" data-end=3D"4616">Plus rapide, API plus moderne, fac=
ile =C3=A0 utiliser que Selenium</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4617" data-end=3D"4692">
<p data-start=3D"4619" data-end=3D"4692">S=E2=80=99int=C3=A8gre bien avec p=
ytest, id=C3=A9al pour des suites de tests plus complexes</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4694" data-end=3D"4697">
<h3 data-start=3D"4699" data-end=3D"4750">C. Bonnes pratiques pour les test=
s fonctionnels</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4752" data-end=3D"5156">
<li data-start=3D"4752" data-end=3D"4845">
<p data-start=3D"4754" data-end=3D"4845">=C3=89vitez les <code data-start=
=3D"4765" data-end=3D"4779">time.sleep()</code>, pr=C3=A9f=C3=A9rez les att=
entes explicites (<code data-start=3D"4815" data-end=3D"4825">wait_for</cod=
e>, <code data-start=3D"4827" data-end=3D"4844">implicitly_wait</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4846" data-end=3D"4917">
<p data-start=3D"4848" data-end=3D"4917">Nettoyez les donn=C3=A9es avant/ap=
r=C3=A8s tests pour =C3=A9viter les effets de bord</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4918" data-end=3D"4998">
<p data-start=3D"4920" data-end=3D"4998">Utilisez des bases de donn=C3=A9es=
 de test sp=C3=A9cifiques (LiveServerTestCase g=C3=A8re =C3=A7a)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4999" data-end=3D"5084">
<p data-start=3D"5001" data-end=3D"5084">Testez les flux principaux : inscr=
iption, connexion, cr=C3=A9ation, =C3=A9dition, suppression</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5085" data-end=3D"5156">
<p data-start=3D"5087" data-end=3D"5156">Automatisez l=E2=80=99ex=C3=A9cuti=
on des tests fonctionnels dans votre pipeline CI</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5158" data-end=3D"5161">
<h2 data-start=3D"5163" data-end=3D"5229">11.6 Int=C3=A9gration continue (C=
I) avec GitHub Actions ou GitLab CI</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"5231" data-end=3D"5234">
<h3 data-start=3D"5236" data-end=3D"5278">Qu=E2=80=99est-ce que l=E2=80=99i=
nt=C3=A9gration continue ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"5280" data-end=3D"5487">L=E2=80=99int=C3=A9gration continu=
e (CI) est une pratique DevOps o=C3=B9 les d=C3=A9veloppeurs int=C3=A8grent=
 r=C3=A9guli=C3=A8rement leur code dans un d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t partag=C3=A9, d=
=C3=A9clenchant automatiquement la compilation, les tests et autres v=C3=A9=
rifications.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"5489" data-end=3D"5492">
<h3 data-start=3D"5494" data-end=3D"5535">Pourquoi utiliser la CI avec Djan=
go ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5537" data-end=3D"5759">
<li data-start=3D"5537" data-end=3D"5596">
<p data-start=3D"5539" data-end=3D"5596">Tester automatiquement =C3=A0 chaq=
ue push, merge, pull request</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5597" data-end=3D"5652">
<p data-start=3D"5599" data-end=3D"5652">D=C3=A9tecter rapidement les bugs =
et erreurs d=E2=80=99int=C3=A9gration</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5653" data-end=3D"5703">
<p data-start=3D"5655" data-end=3D"5703">Automatiser le d=C3=A9ploiement et=
 la qualit=C3=A9 du code</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5704" data-end=3D"5759">
<p data-start=3D"5706" data-end=3D"5759">Faciliter le travail collaboratif =
et la revue de code</p>
</li>
</ul>
