<hr data-start=3D"3401" data-end=3D"3404">
<h3 data-start=3D"3406" data-end=3D"3427">2.5. Explications</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3429" data-end=3D"3751">
<li data-start=3D"3429" data-end=3D"3483">
<p data-start=3D"3431" data-end=3D"3483">La classe <code data-start=3D"3441=
" data-end=3D"3458">ArticleQuerySet</code> =C3=A9tend <code data-start=3D"3=
465" data-end=3D"3482">models.QuerySet</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3484" data-end=3D"3570">
<p data-start=3D"3486" data-end=3D"3570">On d=C3=A9finit une m=C3=A9thode m=
=C3=A9tier <code data-start=3D"3516" data-end=3D"3529">published()</code> q=
ui retourne un nouveau QuerySet filtr=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3571" data-end=3D"3669">
<p data-start=3D"3573" data-end=3D"3669">Le <code data-start=3D"3576" data-=
end=3D"3592">ArticleManager</code> surcharge <code data-start=3D"3603" data=
-end=3D"3619">get_queryset()</code> pour retourner une instance de <code da=
ta-start=3D"3651" data-end=3D"3668">ArticleQuerySet</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3670" data-end=3D"3751">
<p data-start=3D"3672" data-end=3D"3751">On peut ainsi exposer les m=C3=A9t=
hodes du QuerySet dans le manager (<code data-start=3D"3736" data-end=3D"37=
49">published()</code>).</p>
</li>
</ul>
