<h3 data-start=3D"3399" data-end=3D"3420">2.3. Explications</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3422" data-end=3D"3710">
<li data-start=3D"3422" data-end=3D"3511">
<p data-start=3D"3424" data-end=3D"3511">Le d=C3=A9corateur <code data-star=
t=3D"3438" data-end=3D"3449">@receiver</code> relie la fonction au signal <=
code data-start=3D"3478" data-end=3D"3489">post_save</code> de l=E2=80=99=
=C3=A9metteur <code data-start=3D"3504" data-end=3D"3510">User</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3512" data-end=3D"3603">
<p data-start=3D"3514" data-end=3D"3603">L=E2=80=99argument <code data-star=
t=3D"3525" data-end=3D"3534">created</code> indique si c=E2=80=99est une cr=
=C3=A9ation (<code data-start=3D"3566" data-end=3D"3572">True</code>) ou un=
e mise =C3=A0 jour (<code data-start=3D"3594" data-end=3D"3601">False</code=
>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3604" data-end=3D"3710">
<p data-start=3D"3606" data-end=3D"3710">La fonction re=C3=A7oit toujours <=
code data-start=3D"3634" data-end=3D"3642">sender</code> (la classe qui =C3=
=A9met), <code data-start=3D"3665" data-end=3D"3675">instance</code> (l=E2=
=80=99objet concern=C3=A9), et <code data-start=3D"3699" data-end=3D"3709">=
**kwargs</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
