<hr data-start=3D"3065" data-end=3D"3068">
<h2 data-start=3D"3070" data-end=3D"3160">Partie 3 =E2=80=94 Permissions ba=
s=C3=A9es sur les objets (Object-level permissions) (niveau avanc=C3=A9)</h=
2>
<hr data-start=3D"3162" data-end=3D"3165">
<h3 data-start=3D"3167" data-end=3D"3205">3.1. Limites du syst=C3=A8me par =
d=C3=A9faut</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3207" data-end=3D"3359">
<li data-start=3D"3207" data-end=3D"3282">
<p data-start=3D"3209" data-end=3D"3282">Par d=C3=A9faut, Django g=C3=A8re =
les permissions au niveau global (sur le mod=C3=A8le).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3283" data-end=3D"3359">
<p data-start=3D"3285" data-end=3D"3359">On ne peut pas, par d=C3=A9faut, c=
ontr=C3=B4ler l=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s sur une instance sp=C3=A9cifique.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3361" data-end=3D"3364">
<h3 data-start=3D"3366" data-end=3D"3408">3.2. Pourquoi les permissions obj=
ets ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3410" data-end=3D"3525">
<li data-start=3D"3410" data-end=3D"3483">
<p data-start=3D"3412" data-end=3D"3483">Exemple : Un utilisateur peut modi=
fier uniquement ses propres articles.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3484" data-end=3D"3525">
<p data-start=3D"3486" data-end=3D"3525">N=C3=A9cessite un contr=C3=B4le fi=
n par instance.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3527" data-end=3D"3530">
<h3 data-start=3D"3532" data-end=3D"3583">3.3. Impl=C3=A9mentation avec des=
 librairies tierces</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3585" data-end=3D"3681">
<li data-start=3D"3585" data-end=3D"3639">
<p data-start=3D"3587" data-end=3D"3639">Django n=E2=80=99a pas nativement =
les permissions par objet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3640" data-end=3D"3681">
<p data-start=3D"3642" data-end=3D"3681">On utilise souvent <strong data-st=
art=3D"3661" data-end=3D"3680">django-guardian</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
