=A9es de Django.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"329" data-end=3D"332">
<h1 data-start=3D"334" data-end=3D"394">12.6 Django avanc=C3=A9 =E2=80=94 M=
ulti-sites et multi-bases de donn=C3=A9es</h1>
<hr data-start=3D"396" data-end=3D"399">
<h2 data-start=3D"401" data-end=3D"416">Introduction</h2>
<p data-start=3D"418" data-end=3D"506">Dans des projets Django complexes ou=
 =C3=A0 grande =C3=A9chelle, il est fr=C3=A9quent de devoir g=C3=A9rer :</p=
>
<ul data-start=3D"508" data-end=3D"654">
<li data-start=3D"508" data-end=3D"579">
<p data-start=3D"510" data-end=3D"579"><strong data-start=3D"510" data-end=
=3D"533">Plusieurs sites web</strong> dans une m=C3=AAme instance Django (m=
ulti-sites)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"580" data-end=3D"654">
<p data-start=3D"582" data-end=3D"654"><strong data-start=3D"582" data-end=
=3D"612">Plusieurs bases de donn=C3=A9es</strong> dans une m=C3=AAme applic=
ation (multi-bases)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"656" data-end=3D"778">Ces deux concepts sont souvent li=C3=
=A9s =C3=A0 la scalabilit=C3=A9, =C3=A0 la s=C3=A9paration des donn=C3=A9es=
 ou =C3=A0 la gestion de clients diff=C3=A9rents.</p>
<p data-start=3D"780" data-end=3D"859">Ce tutoriel vous guidera du niveau d=
=C3=A9butant =C3=A0 expert sur ces deux th=C3=A9matiques :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"861" data-end=3D"1068">
<li data-start=3D"861" data-end=3D"920">
<p data-start=3D"863" data-end=3D"920">Qu=E2=80=99est-ce que le multi-site =
et comment Django le g=C3=A8re ?</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"921" data-end=3D"996">
<p data-start=3D"923" data-end=3D"996">Comment configurer et utiliser plusi=
eurs bases de donn=C3=A9es dans Django ?</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"997" data-end=3D"1068">
<p data-start=3D"999" data-end=3D"1068">Comment combiner ces deux concepts =
pour des architectures robustes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1070" data-end=3D"1073">
<h1 data-start=3D"1075" data-end=3D"1145">Partie 1 =E2=80=94 Multi-sites av=
ec Django (niveau d=C3=A9butant =C3=A0 interm=C3=A9diaire)</h1>
<hr data-start=3D"1147" data-end=3D"1150">
<h3 data-start=3D"1152" data-end=3D"1191">1.1. Qu=E2=80=99est-ce que le mul=
ti-sites ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1193" data-end=3D"1419">Le <strong data-start=3D"1196" dat=
a-end=3D"1211">multi-sites</strong> consiste =C3=A0 g=C3=A9rer plusieurs si=
tes web distincts (ex: <code data-start=3D"1264" data-end=3D"1277">monsite.=
com</code>, <code data-start=3D"1279" data-end=3D"1291">monsite.fr</code>, =
<code data-start=3D"1293" data-end=3D"1311">blog.monsite.com</code>) avec l=
a m=C3=AAme instance Django, souvent en partageant la m=C3=AAme base de don=
n=C3=A9es ou avec des donn=C3=A9es partag=C3=A9es.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1421" data-end=3D"1439">C=E2=80=99est utile pour :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1441" data-end=3D"1636">
<li data-start=3D"1441" data-end=3D"1531">
<p data-start=3D"1443" data-end=3D"1531">Projets multi-domaines (ex: sites =
dans diff=C3=A9rentes langues ou pour diff=C3=A9rents clients)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1532" data-end=3D"1581">
<p data-start=3D"1534" data-end=3D"1581">Gestion centralis=C3=A9e d=E2=80=
=99applications similaires</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1582" data-end=3D"1636">
<p data-start=3D"1584" data-end=3D"1636">R=C3=A9duction de la maintenance e=
n mutualisant le code</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1638" data-end=3D"1641">
<h3 data-start=3D"1643" data-end=3D"1687">1.2. Le framework <code data-star=
t=3D"1665" data-end=3D"1687">django.contrib.sites</code></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1689" data-end=3D"1865">Django inclut un framework de base=
 pour le multi-sites dans l=E2=80=99app <code data-start=3D"1755" data-end=
=3D"1777">django.contrib.sites</code>. Ce framework fournit un mod=C3=A8le =
<code data-start=3D"1810" data-end=3D"1816">Site</code> permettant de diff=
=C3=A9rencier les donn=C3=A9es par site.</p>
