<h2 data-start=3D"3474" data-end=3D"3527">=F0=9F=A7=A0 18.5 Int=C3=A9gratio=
n avec GraphQL (Graphene-Django)</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"3529" data-end=3D"3532">
<h3 data-start=3D"3534" data-end=3D"3559">=F0=9F=94=8E Pourquoi GraphQL ?</=
h3>
<p data-start=3D"3561" data-end=3D"3597">GraphQL est une alternative =C3=A0=
 REST :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3598" data-end=3D"3821">
<li data-start=3D"3598" data-end=3D"3662">
<p data-start=3D"3600" data-end=3D"3662">Une seule <strong data-start=3D"36=
10" data-end=3D"3634">entr=C3=A9e (<code data-start=3D"3620" data-end=3D"36=
31">/graphql/</code>)</strong> pour toutes les ressources,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3663" data-end=3D"3718">
<p data-start=3D"3665" data-end=3D"3718">Le client <strong data-start=3D"36=
75" data-end=3D"3697">choisit les champs</strong> qu=E2=80=99il veut recevo=
ir,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3719" data-end=3D"3789">
<p data-start=3D"3721" data-end=3D"3789">Moins de requ=C3=AAtes HTTP (r=C3=
=A9cup=C3=A9ration en profondeur d=E2=80=99une ressource),</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3790" data-end=3D"3821">
<p data-start=3D"3792" data-end=3D"3821">Typage fort et introspection.</p>
</li>
</ul>
